.TH "INSPEKT\-TUNNEL" "1" "2026\-04\-16" "Inspekt 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
inspekt\-tunnel \- Expose a local port to the Inspekt Browser VM.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]inspekt\f[R] \f[B]tunnel\f[R] [\f[I]OPTIONS\f[R]] \f[I]PORT\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Expose a local port to the Inspekt Browser VM.
.PP
Makes your local development server accessible from within the VM\(cqs
browser.
Run this on your local machine while the VM is running.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\f[I]PORT\f[R]
required integer argument
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\(enhost\f[R], \f[I]HOST\f[R]
VM host address (default: localhost for local VM).
.TP
\f[B]\(ensecret\f[R], \f[I]SECRET\f[R]
Tunnel secret (auto\-detected from VM if not specified).
.TP
\f[B]\(enremote\-port\f[R], \f[I]PORT\f[R]
Port on VM side (default: same as local port).
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
inspekt tunnel 3000
inspekt tunnel 8080 \-\-host vm.example.com
inspekt tunnel 3000 \-\-remote\-port 8000
.EE
